        "original_id": "1d607b01-0502-5a78-baca-e07f2e533cdc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Windermere, Cumbria; Bowness-on-Windermere; England\n- Organizations: Windermere Hotel\n- Topics: Windermere railway station; railway link with Kendal\n\nFacts:\n- In 1847, the railway link with Kendal was established.\n- In 1847, the town of Windermere took the name of the lake when the railway line was built and the station was called \"Windermere.\"\n- In 1847, Windermere Hotel, originally called The Riggs Windermere, opened near Windermere railway station in Windermere, Cumbria, England.\n- The town of Windermere does not touch the lake named Windermere.\n- Windermere has grown together with the older lakeside town of Bowness-on-Windermere, but the two towns still have distinguishable town centres.",
